			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4073330">
									

<p>The community will upvote what it likes. Currently, people seem to be jonesing for short, interesting, Series-I-style articles; therefore, it's up to authors to provide them that. We'll always have long articles, and we'll always have short articles, and it's good to have a mix of both that prevents the site from becoming stuck in a role.</p>
<p>Regarding this one&#8230; I can't think of anything to add that would make it better. It's scary on a fundamental level, partly because of the brevity; it uses the reader's own imaginations to more effectively induce emotion. That's not &quot;unfinished concept&quot;, that's &quot;calculated work of fiction&quot;.</p>
<p>That said, maybe I'm just not good enough at expanding works. If <em>you've</em> got a suggestion, I'd love to hear it :)</p>

