<p>None of the successful short articles the community has produced are anything like game demos, unless you can somehow demonstrate where they're being used to give a demonstration of a larger work for someone to purchase. They're no more &quot;demos&quot; for long-form articles than a minimalist painting is a &quot;demo&quot; for an exhaustively-detailed fresco. They're complete works.</p>
<p>If anything, I can agree that this lacks a traditional &quot;narrative&quot; &#8212; even by SCP article standard &#8212; but formulaic construction and closure isn't the intent here: This is a tableau.</p>
<p>I am interested in how you think short works are going to actually <em>harm</em> the site. It's not an opinion I've seen anyone express anywhere else, so I am curious as to whatever unique insight you possess that would cause you to make such a bold claim.</p>

